---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageLead from "../components/PageLead.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice — AnalyseSpider"
  description="How the current AnalyseSpider website handles hosting requests, browser-local tool input, email contact, external links, and data-subject rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <PageLead
    title="Privacy follows the actual data path"
    intro="The current tools work locally in your browser. Hosting requests, email contact, and links are separate boundaries and are described here without claiming that all internet infrastructure is storage-free."
  />
  <section class="content-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Controller</h2>
      <p><strong>{site.operator.name}</strong><br />{site.operator.streetAddress}<br />{site.operator.postalCode} {site.operator.addressLocality}<br />Germany</p>
      <p>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.operator.email}`}>{site.operator.email}</a><br />Telephone: <a href="tel:+4917642449858">{site.operator.telephone}</a></p>

      <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
      <p>AnalyseSpider is hosted and delivered through Vercel. When you request a page, your browser necessarily sends connection and request metadata to the hosting infrastructure. This can include the IP address, timestamp, requested URL, HTTP method and status, referrer, user agent, and security-related request information.</p>
      <p>This processing is used to deliver the website, maintain availability, prevent abuse, and diagnose technical failures. Hosting-level processing and retention are governed by the applicable Vercel configuration and service terms. It is separate from the contents you paste into the current diagnostic tools.</p>

      <h2>Browser-local diagnostic tools</h2>
      <p>The Log File Inspector, Response Inspector, and IP Address Check run as browser-local JavaScript. The current application does not upload the selected log file, pasted response, entered IP address, or generated result to an AnalyseSpider application endpoint. It does not fetch a URL entered by a visitor.</p>
      <p>The input can still remain in your device memory, clipboard, browser history or extensions, screenshots, and any files you export or save. Redact confidential logs before using any diagnostic tool, including a local one.</p>

      <h2>Cookies, analytics, and accounts</h2>
      <p><strong>No analytics</strong>, advertising pixels, behavioral tracking, account system, or profiling service is currently integrated. <strong>No application cookies</strong> are set by the current site. There is no newsletter signup, payment flow, or user account.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><strong>No contact form</strong> is embedded on this website. Clicking an email link opens your chosen email service. If you contact the operator, the email address, message, headers, attachments, and follow-up correspondence are processed to answer the request, document rights or security concerns, and meet applicable legal obligations. Do not send passwords, raw customer data, private logs, or former software files.</p>

      <h2>External links and public repository</h2>
      <p>AnalyseSpider links to standards, search-platform documentation, source projects, Contextter, and the public GitHub repository. No external page is embedded automatically. When you follow a link, the destination receives the normal request information and applies its own privacy terms.</p>
      <p>The Google Search Console ownership TXT record is a DNS verification record. It does not add an analytics script or transmit visitor tool input.</p>

      <h2>Retention and recipients</h2>
      <p>The current AnalyseSpider application does not create a database record for page visitors or tool input. Technical request information can be processed by the hosting provider, and email correspondence by the involved email providers. Information is retained only as needed for delivery, security, correspondence, evidence of handled requests, or legal obligations, subject to provider and account settings.</p>

      <h2>Your data-subject rights</h2>
      <p>Where the GDPR applies, a data subject can request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, or object to processing, subject to the statutory conditions. A complaint can also be made to a competent data-protection supervisory authority. Send privacy requests to <a href={`mailto:${site.operator.email}?subject=AnalyseSpider%20privacy`}>{site.operator.email}</a>.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>This notice describes the current static, browser-local implementation as reviewed on 22 August 2026. A future analytics service, server-side fetcher, upload, account, billing flow, or additional processor requires an updated technical and privacy review before activation.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="side-note">
      <h3>Current declaration</h3>
      <dl class="facts-list">
        <div><dt>Hosting</dt><dd>Vercel</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tool processing</dt><dd>Browser-local</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tool upload</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Analytics</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        <div><dt>App cookies</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Contact form</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Accounts</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Updated</dt><dd>22 August 2026</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
